{"key":"enterprise/T1016","id":"T1016","name":"System Network Configuration Discovery","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["discovery"],"platforms":["ESXi","Linux","macOS","Network Devices","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may look for details about the network configuration and settings, such as IP and/or MAC addresses, of systems they access or through information discovery of remote systems. Several operating system administration utilities exist that can be used to gather this information. Examples include Arp, ipconfig/ifconfig, nbtstat, and route. Adversaries may also leverage a Network Device CLI on network devices to gather information about…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1016","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--707399d6-ab3e-4963-9315-d9d3818cd6a0","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.641Z","source_object_version":"1.7","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0195","name":"Behavioral Detection of System Network Configuration Discovery","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0195","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--172cff54-a89b-4207-abc2-8d0c9601025e","relationship_id":"relationship--229b177b-8a94-4206-b6d9-9c295604df22"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0559","name":"Analytic 0559","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0195#AN0559","guidance":"Execution of built-in tools (e.g., ipconfig, route, netsh) or PowerShell/WMI queries to enumerate IP, MAC, interface status, or routing configuration.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0195"},{"id":"AN0560","name":"Analytic 0560","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0195#AN0560","guidance":"Execution of `ifconfig`, `ip a`, or access to `/proc/net/` indicating collection of local interface and route configuration.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0195"},{"id":"AN0561","name":"Analytic 0561","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0195#AN0561","guidance":"Execution of `ifconfig`, `networksetup`, or `system_profiler` to query IP/MAC/interface configuration and status.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0195"},{"id":"AN0562","name":"Analytic 0562","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0195#AN0562","guidance":"Use of `esxcli network` commands (e.g., `esxcli network nic list`, `esxcli network ip interface ipv4 get`) via SSH or hostd to enumerate adapter and IP information.","platforms":["ESXi"],"strategy_id":"DET0195"},{"id":"AN0563","name":"Analytic 0563","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0195#AN0563","guidance":"CLI-based execution of interface and routing discovery commands (e.g., `show ip interface`, `show arp`, `show route`) over Telnet, SSH, or console.","platforms":["Network Devices"],"strategy_id":"DET0195"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0559","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0195#AN0559","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0064","component":"Command Execution","name":"WinEventLog:PowerShell","channel":"EventCode=4103, 4104, 4105, 4106","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0559","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0195#AN0559","validation":"upstream_definition_not_