on.com/blog/dropping-anchor-from-a-trickbot-infection-to-the-discovery-of-the-anchor-malware"},{"title":"Strategic Cyber LLC. (2020, November 5). Cobalt Strike: Advanced Threat Tactics for Penetration Testers. Retrieved April 13, 2021.","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210708035426/https://www.cobaltstrike.com/downloads/csmanual43.pdf"}]}]},{"id":"S0488","name":"CrackMapExec","page":"tools/S0488/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--de55c190-81ee-49b8-a279-1692725ea6cc","description":"CrackMapExec can collect DNS information from the targeted system.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0488","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"byt3bl33d3r. (2018, September 8). SMB: Command Reference. Retrieved July 17, 2020.","url":"https://github.com/byt3bl33d3r/CrackMapExec/wiki/SMB-Command-Reference"}]}]},{"id":"S0363","name":"Empire","page":"tools/S0363/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--07db5f41-fc53-47e6-ae7b-755a4acc9e62","description":"Empire can acquire network configuration information like DNS servers, public IP, and network proxies used by a host.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0363","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Adamitis, D. et al. (2019, June 4). It's alive: Threat actors cobble together open-source pieces into monstrous Frankenstein campaign. Retrieved May 11, 2020.","url":"https://blog.talosintelligence.com/2019/06/frankenstein-campaign.html"},{"title":"Schroeder, W., Warner, J., Nelson, M. (n.d.). Github PowerShellEmpire. Retrieved April 28, 2016.","url":"https://github.com/PowerShellEmpire/Empire"}]}]},{"id":"S9003","name":"evilginx2","page":"tools/S9003/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--cf5cb40e-9857-438c-8e57-26088a87e879","description":"evilginx2 can capture information from each session with a victim including the public IP used to access the server and the user agent.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S9003","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Everts, M. (2025, March 28). Stealing user credentials with evilginx. Retrieved January 27, 2026.","url":"https://www.sophos.com/en-us/blog/stealing-user-credentials-with-evilginx"}]}]},{"id":"S0101","name":"ifconfig","page":"tools/S0101/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--01e01c24-ba4c-41d7-8f30-8fca364dc2c6","description":"ifconfig can be used to display adapter configuration on Unix systems, including information for TCP/IP, DNS, and DHCP.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0101","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[]}]},{"id":"S0100","name":"ipconfig","page":"tools/S0100/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--b91e06c1-9546-4184-9552-ba501bf9182e","description":"ipconfig can be used to display adapter configuration on Windows systems, including information for TCP/IP, DNS, and DHCP.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0100","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[]}]},{"id":"S0250","name":"Koadic","page":"tools/S0250/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--03be081b-574e-4ffd-807a-99163b6a6fa2","description":"Koadic can retrieve the contents of the IP routing table as well as information about the Windows domain.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0250","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Jazi, H. (2021, February). LazyScripter: From Empire to double RAT. Retrieved November 