ol","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--269bab05-022c-4fb8-bdf3-1ec721ff994e","description":"PcShare can obtain the proxy settings of a compromised machine using `InternetQueryOptionA` and its IP address by running `nslookup myip.opendns.comresolver1.opendns.com\\r\\n`.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1050","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Vrabie, V. (2020, November). Dissecting a Chinese APT Targeting South Eastern Asian Government Institutions. Retrieved September 19, 2022.","url":"https://www.bitdefender.com/files/News/CaseStudies/study/379/Bitdefender-Whitepaper-Chinese-APT.pdf"}]}]},{"id":"S0378","name":"PoshC2","page":"tools/S0378/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--092b3643-670d-447c-b05d-f7a54a945412","description":"PoshC2 can enumerate network adapter information.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0378","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Nettitude. (2018, July 23). Python Server for PoshC2. Retrieved April 23, 2019.","url":"https://github.com/nettitude/PoshC2_Python"}]}]},{"id":"S0192","name":"Pupy","page":"tools/S0192/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relationship_id":"relationship--4d8fd7fc-eb0b-4031-8df0-ef3d237edb7c","description":"Pupy has built in commands to identify a host’s IP address and find out other network configuration settings by viewing connected sessions.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0192","source_commit":"6cda5ad8462c79e14fbb872f4e09059b18e0cfc4","citations":[{"title":"Nicolas Verdier. (n.d.). Retrieved January 29, 2018.","url":"https://github.com/n1nj4sec/pupy"}]}]},{"id":"S0262","name":"QuasarRAT","page":"tools/S0262/","kind":"attack_tool","bases":["attack_uses"],"evidence":[{"basis":"attack_uses","relations